  [smyth2007] [3] Smyth B. Adventures in personalized information access. In: Conati C, McCoy K, editors. User Modeling 2007, Berlin: Springer; 2007, pp. 5–6. https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-74958-5_4.
  [vangogh2020] [4] van Gogh V, The Accessible Reading Group. Screen readers and the reading of mathematics. In:. Proceedings of the Conference on Accessible Reading, Accessible Press; 2020, pp. 101–10.
  [muller2019] [5] Müller J. Hörbücher und Sprachsynthese. PhD thesis. Universität Wien, 2019.
  [who2021] [6] World Health Organization. World report on vision & print disability. Geneva: World Health Organization; 2021.
  [access2024] [7] Doe J. Designing for keyboard and screen reader users. Accessibility Notes 2024. https://example.org/notes/keyboard (accessed September 1, 2026).
